-### Rasterization Steps
-
-1. **Projection and Tile Assignment:**
-   Project the eight corner points of each voxel into screen space [S1]. Determine the axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) of these projected points [S1]. Assign the voxel to all tiles that overlap with this AABB [S1].
-
-2. **Pre-processing:**
-   For each active voxel assigned to tiles, compute shared properties:
-   - **Color:** Approximate view-dependent color using SH coefficients evaluated at the direction from camera to voxel center $\mathbf{v}_c$ [S1]:
-     $$
-     c = \max(0, \text{sh\_eval}(\mathbf{v}_{\text{sh}}, \text{normalize}(\mathbf{v}_c - \mathbf{r}_o)))
-     $$
-   - **Normal:** Compute the analytical gradient of the density field at the voxel center $\mathbf{q}_c = (0.5, 0.5, 0.5)$ [S1]:
-     $$
-     \mathbf{n} = \text{normalize} (\nabla_{\mathbf{q}} \text{interp} (\mathbf{V}, \mathbf{q}_c))
-     $$
-     The unnormalized gradient is:
-     $$
-     \nabla_{\mathbf{q}} \text{interp}(\mathbf{V}, \mathbf{q}^{(c)}) = 0.25 \cdot \begin{bmatrix} (\mathbf{V}_{100} + \mathbf{V}_{101} + \mathbf{V}_{110} + \mathbf{V}_{111}) - (\mathbf{V}_{000} + \mathbf{V}_{001} + \mathbf{V}_{010} + \mathbf{V}_{011}) \\ (\mathbf{V}_{010} + \mathbf{V}_{011} + \mathbf{V}_{110} + \mathbf{V}_{111}) - (\mathbf{V}_{000} + \mathbf{V}_{001} + \mathbf{V}_{100} + \mathbf{V}_{101}) \\ (\mathbf{V}_{001} + \mathbf{V}_{011} + \mathbf{V}_{101} + \mathbf{V}_{111}) - (\mathbf{V}_{000} + \mathbf{V}_{010} + \mathbf{V}_{100} + \mathbf{V}_{110}) \end{bmatrix}
-     $$
-
-3. **Sorting:**
-   Sort voxels within each tile to ensure correct front-to-back rendering order [S1].
-   - Use direction-dependent Morton order [S1]. The permutation of the Morton code depends on the signs of the ray direction components (8 permutations for 3D space) [S1].
-   - This ensures that voxels from different octree levels are sorted correctly relative to the camera [S1].
-   - Incorrect sorting (e.g., by center distance) causes popping artifacts [S1].
-
-4. **Ray-Voxel Intersection:**
-   For each pixel in a tile, cast a ray [S1]. Intersect the ray with each assigned voxel to determine the entry $a$ and exit $b$ distances [S1]:
